{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CesYHNRW3oeQDkcjuyUqg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment model with status enum (Shipment.kt:9-27): CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- ShipmentController with create/get/list endpoints (ShipmentController.kt:26-56)\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository (ShipmentRepository.kt:15-22): save() and findById()\n- ApiException types: ConflictException (409) at ApiExceptions.kt:22-24 and ResourceNotFoundException (404) at ApiExceptions.kt:18-20\n- GlobalExceptionHandler converts exceptions to error responses (GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28)\n- ErrorCode enum (ApiError.kt:31-37) with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND and SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS\n- Existing tests in ShipmentControllerTest.kt show MockMvc patterns\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Endpoints throw ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler catches them\n- POST creation returns 201 with HttpStatus.CREATED; other endpoints return 200\n- Error codes come from a closed ErrorCode enum\n- Controllers inject repository and call save()/findById() directly\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions for verification\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` — add POST /{shipmentId}/confirm method\n2. `ApiError.kt` — add SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED error code to enum (required for 409 response)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — add test cases for new endpoint\n\n**Risks:**\n- Idempotency: if already confirmed, request must succeed without changes; if not, operation fails twice\n- Error code must exist in enum or code won't compile\n- Status code must be 200 (OK) not 201 (CREATED) since it's not creating a new resource\n\n**Open questions:** None. Requirement is clear about all cases.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED` to the ErrorCode enum. This is necessary to provide a machine-readable error code for the 409 response when confirming a cancelled shipment, consistent with existing error codes.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add method `confirm(shipmentId: String)` with:\n   - `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")`\n   - Find shipment by ID; if not found, throw ResourceNotFoundException with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND (404)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED (409)\n   - If status is already CONFIRMED, return it unchanged (idempotent, 200)\n   - If status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED, save, return with 200\n   - Return ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) in all success cases\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add five test cases:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment and returns CONFIRMED status` — verify state transition from CREATED to CONFIRMED\n   - `idempotently confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment` — verify retry succeeds without change\n   - `rejects confirmation of a CANCELLED shipment` — verify 409 with error code\n   - `rejects confirmation of non-existent shipment` — verify 404 with error code\n   - `persists confirmed shipment to repository` — verify subsequent GET retrieves confirmed status\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Returning 204 No Content (not 200 with body): The requirement says \"returns the shipment\", so body is required.\n- Reusing an existing error code for cancelled case: SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED is more semantic and consistent with SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS.\n- Adding a separate confirm service layer: Simpler to follow the pattern of create/get (direct repository use in controller).\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\nFor each case the ticket names:\n\n| Case | Input | Read | Logic | Write | Response |\n|------|-------|------|-------|-------|----------|\n| CREATED→CONFIRMED | shipmentId | repository.findById() | copy with CONFIRMED | repository.save(copied) | 200 OK with shipment |\n| Already CONFIRMED | shipmentId | repository.findById() | check status == CONFIRMED | none | 200 OK with shipment (idempotent) |\n| CANCELLED state | shipmentId | repository.findById() | check status == CANCELLED | none | 409 ConflictException (error code) |\n| Not found | shipmentId | repository.findById() returns null | null check | none | 404 ResourceNotFoundException (error code) |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nEach test case covers one path through the confirm logic:\n\n1. **Happy path (CREATED→CONFIRMED)**: Create shipment, confirm it, verify status changed to CONFIRMED\n2. **Idempotency**: Confirm twice, verify second call returns 200 and status unchanged\n3. **Cancelled rejection**: Insert cancelled shipment directly to repository, try confirm, verify 409 with SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED code\n4. **Not found**: Call confirm on non-existent ID, verify 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n5. **Persistence**: Create, confirm, then GET to verify it persisted as CONFIRMED\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nFirst, add the error code to the ErrorCode enum:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1140,"cache_read_input_tokens":19982,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1140},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff719be6-a375-4059-adb7-5ffa2d5a87b0","uuid":"62a3ba27-9f0a-4185-8ee5-177c14807b3f","timestamp":"2026-09-09T08:21:13.549Z","request_id":"req_011CesYHMh6J9ZfkPCxarGjh"}
